-- statement:
--   For a complex Hilbert space H and a unital complex star subalgebra S of the bounded linear operators on H, WOTClosed(S) means that S is closed in the weak operator topology. For a set s of operators, wstar(s) is the intersection of all weak-operator-closed star subalgebras containing s, thus the weak-operator-closed star subalgebra generated by s. IsII1Factor(S) is a defined proposition whose fields require that the zero and identity operators on H differ, that S is weak-operator closed, that every element of S commuting with every element of S is a scalar multiple of the identity, and that every isometry in S is unitary: v* v = 1 implies v v* = 1. It also requires diffuseness: every nonzero self-adjoint projection p in S has a nonzero self-adjoint projection q in S with q ≠ p and pq = qp = q. HasSeparablePredual(S) means that there exists a separable complex Banach space X whose continuous dual, equipped with its operator norm, is conjugate-linearly isometrically equivalent to S. Finally, SinglyGenerated(S) means that there is an operator x in S for which wstar({x}) = S; the generator is not required to be self-adjoint.
